## Direct recommendation

Add a **single bulk-write method** to the files API module (`writeMultiple`) that mirrors the existing `upload-multiple` naming convention, then drive it from the files view with a per-`CodeViewer` checkbox + a sticky “Save N files” action. I can only apply the API half here — the files view file isn't in my context yet.

---

## Specifications

| Area | Decision |
|---|---|
| Endpoint | `POST /api/files/write-multiple` — consistent with existing `/api/files/upload-multiple` |
| Payload | `{ files: [{ path, content }] }` — array keeps ordering and makes partial-error reporting easy |
| Return | Per-file results so the view can mark only failed editors: `{ results: [{ path, ok, error }] }` |
| Selection state | Lives in the view (`data.selectedPaths: []`), not in `CodeViewer` (keeps the presenter dumb) |
| Save trigger | One button, disabled when `selectedPaths.length === 0` or while `saving` |
| Feedback | Per-editor success/error badge + one global toast; never a silent no-op |
| Dirty guard | Only send editors whose content differs from the last saved snapshot |

---

## File change

