## Implementation steps for the files view (needs the file)

Send me the view file (e.g. `src/views/FilesView.vue` / whatever hosts the `CodeViewer` list) and I'll apply this exact pattern:

1. **`data()`** → `selectedPaths: []`, `saving: false`, `saveResult: null`.
2. **Selection toggle** on each editor row:
   ```html
   <input
     type="checkbox"
     class="checkbox checkbox-xs checkbox-primary"
     :checked="isSelected(file.path)"
     :aria-label="`Select ${file.path}`"
     @change="toggleSelection(file.path)"
   />
   ```
3. **`toggleSelection(path)`** → push/splice `selectedPaths` (use a `Set` internally for O(1) lookups on 1000+ rows).
4. **Shift-click range select** between the last clicked index and the current one — the expected power-user behaviour, and it costs ~10 lines.
5. **Bulk save action** — sticky footer bar, only rendered when `selectedPaths.length > 0`:
   ```html
   <div class="sticky bottom-0 z-30 flex items-center gap-3 px-4 py-2 bg-base-100 border-t border-base-content/10">
     <span class="text-xs text-base-content/60">{{ selectedPaths.length }} selected</span>
     <button class="btn btn-sm btn-primary gap-1" :disabled="saving" @click="saveSelected">
       <span v-if="saving" class="loading loading-spinner loading-xs"></span>
       <i v-else class="fa-solid fa-floppy-disk"></i>
       Save {{ selectedPaths.length }} file{{ selectedPaths.length > 1 ? 's' : '' }}
     </button>
   </div>
   ```
6. **`saveSelected()`** → filter to dirty editors, call `this.$api.files.writeMultiple(payload)`, then map `response.results` back onto each editor to show a per-file ✓/✗ badge and clear only the successful ones from the selection.

---

## Clarifying questions (blocking a full implementation)

1. **Path of the files view** that renders the `CodeViewer` instances — I won't overwrite a file I can't see.
2. **Exact contract of the new endpoint** — I assumed `POST /api/files/write-multiple` with `{ files: [{ path, content }] }`. If the backend accepted `{ path, page_content, metadata }` per item (like `write`), say so and I'll match it precisely.

---

## Anti-patterns to avoid here

- ❌ **Fire-and-forget saving** — a bulk save *must* report which file failed, otherwise the user silently loses an edit.
- ❌ **Disabling the save button without a reason** — if nothing is dirty, show “No changes” instead of a dead grey button.
- ❌ **Selection living inside `CodeViewer`** — the editor becomes stateful, gets hard to reuse, and “select all” becomes an N-emitter dance.

